        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A cube of side \\(a\\) has a tetrahedral cavity removed. The four vertices of the cavity are four alternate vertices of the cube, so that the cavity is a regular tetrahedron. The volume of the remaining solid is",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The edge of the regular tetrahedron is the face diagonal of the cube, namely \\(a\\sqrt2\\). Thus its volume is \\(\\frac{(a\\sqrt2)^3}{6\\sqrt2}=\\frac{a^3}{3}\\). The remaining volume is \\(a^3-\\frac{a^3}{3}=\\frac{2a^3}{3}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
