        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A regular square pyramid of base side \\(a\\) and height \\(a\\) is erected externally on the top face of a cube of side \\(a\\). The ratio of the volume of the resulting solid to its exposed surface area is",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The pyramid's slant height is \\(\\ell=\\sqrt{a^2+(a/2)^2}=\\frac{a\\sqrt5}{2}\\). Its lateral area is \\(2a\\ell=a^2\\sqrt5\\). The cube contributes \\(5a^2\\) to the exposed area, so \\(S=a^2(5+\\sqrt5)\\). The total volume is \\(a^3+\\frac13a^2\\cdot a=\\frac{4a^3}{3}\\). Therefore \\(V/S=\\frac{4a}{3(5+\\sqrt5)}\\).",
